  "body": "## Summary\nOpenClaw Companion v2026.9.9-alpha.36 can disable the \u201cInstall a local native gateway\u201d option while presenting an Insider build requirement that is already satisfied by the current Windows build. The message does not identify the failed capability check or provide useful remediation.\n\n## Environment\n- Lenovo Yoga 9 2-in-1 16N1X11 (NVIDIA RTX Spark N1X), Windows ARM64\n- Windows 11 Pro 26H1, build 28000.2956\n- OpenClaw Companion v2026.9.9-alpha.36 (ARM64)\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n1. Launch Companion on the above system.\n2. Open the first-run Gateway setup choice page.\n3. Observe Native Gateway disabled and read the guidance.\n\n## Expected\nWhen native support is unavailable, identify the failed capability/feature check and give remediation applicable to the current build.\n\n## Actual\nThe UI says: \u201cNative gateway support is unavailable. Install Windows Insider build 26340.9212 or a newer supported build in Windows Update, then reopen this page. Feature availability can vary by device.\u201d The machine was already on build 28000.2956. A Companion capability probe reported `probes.isolationSessionAvailable=false`; source review indicates the gate depends on this probe rather than a simple build comparison. After Windows updated to build 28000.3231, the option became enabled; the reason for the change is unknown.\n\nInternal tracking: [NVBug 6941780](https://nvbugspro.nvidia.com/bug/6941780).",
